%% Tool Scoping — session type + capabilities + write-through to SessionInfo
%% How tools are computed, delivered, and updated across all contexts.

sequenceDiagram
    participant info as SessionInfo
    participant compute as computeTools<br/>ForSession
    participant surface as tool-surface.ts
    participant transport as bridge-<br/>transport.ts
    participant bridge as bridge.ts
    participant cc as Claude Code<br/>session

    Note over info: Identity fields:<br/>sessionType: master_orchestrator / thread_owner / thread_guest / factory_builder<br/>capabilities: Capability[] (additive grants: protocol_context, factory)<br/>toolDescriptions: Record (phase-specific)<br/>toolInputSchemas: Record (phase-specific)

    Note over compute: Pure function:<br/>BASE_TOOLS[sessionType] ∪ CAPABILITY_TOOLS[each capability]<br/>→ filter UNIVERSAL_TOOLS<br/>→ apply description + schema overrides

    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        Note over info,cc: SPAWN — session created
        info->>info: sessionType set at spawn (determines base tools)
        Note over surface: getToolsForSession reads SessionInfo
        surface->>compute: (type, caps, overrides?)
        compute-->>surface: tool list
        surface->>transport: registered msg with tools
        transport->>bridge: {type: registered, tools, sessionMetadata}
        bridge->>cc: notifications/tools/list_changed
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 240)
        Note over info,cc: PROTOCOL PHASE TRANSITION — actor changes
        Note over info: setProtocolTools(run, sessionId)
        info->>info: Clear protocol keys (advance, extend_phase)
        info->>info: Active actor: addCapability('protocol_context')<br/>+ descriptions + schema (verdict stripped/required per phase)
        info->>info: Previous actor: removeCapability('protocol_context')<br/>+ removeToolDescriptions + removeToolInputSchemas
        loop for each participant
            surface->>compute: (type, caps, overrides?)
            compute-->>surface: tool list
            surface->>transport: {type: tools_update, tools}
            transport->>bridge: tools_update
            bridge->>cc: notifications/tools/list_changed
        end
    end

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over info,cc: FACTORY PHASE TRANSITION
        Note over info: transitionFactoryPhase → setFactoryTools
        info->>info: Description-only: factory_done description<br/>changes per phase (building / reviewing / awaiting_pm)
        surface->>compute: (type, caps, overrides?)
        compute-->>surface: tool list
        surface->>transport: {type: tools_update, tools}
        transport->>bridge: tools_update
        bridge->>cc: notifications/tools/list_changed
    end

    rect rgb(248, 240, 255)
        Note over info,cc: BRIDGE RECONNECT — no derivation
        Note over info: SessionInfo already correct<br/>(written at last transition, persisted)
        surface->>compute: (type, caps, overrides?)
        compute-->>surface: tool list
        surface->>transport: registered msg with tools
        transport->>bridge: {type: registered, tools, sessionMetadata}
        bridge->>cc: notifications/tools/list_changed
    end

    rect rgb(255, 240, 240)
        Note over info,cc: PROTOCOL COMPLETE / CANCEL
        Note over info: clearProtocolOverrides(info)
        info->>info: removeCapability('protocol_context')<br/>+ removeToolDescriptions('advance', 'extend_phase')<br/>+ removeToolInputSchemas('advance')
        surface->>transport: tools_update (restored to base set)
    end

    rect rgb(245, 245, 245)
        Note over info,cc: FACTORY CLEANUP
        Note over info: clearFactoryIdentity(info)
        info->>info: sessionType → thread_owner<br/>+ removeToolDescriptions('factory_done')
        surface->>transport: tools_update (session restored to thread_owner base)
    end

    rect rgb(255, 250, 230)
        Note over info,cc: PULL — tools/list, and why it must not announce itself
        Note over bridge,cc: Every section above is a PUSH: the daemon has news,<br/>and list_changed is how the client hears it.<br/>This one runs the other way, and that reverses the rule.
        cc->>bridge: tools/list
        bridge->>transport: {type: request_tools}
        Note over transport: floor: a second ask inside 1s goes unanswered,<br/>so a looping client times out and falls back to cache
        transport->>surface: getToolsForSession(sessionId)
        surface->>compute: (type, caps, overrides?)
        compute-->>surface: tool list
        surface->>transport: {type: tools_update, tools}
        transport->>bridge: tools_update
        bridge-->>cc: tools/list result (resolves the pending pull)
        Note over bridge,cc: NO list_changed here. The answer is not news to<br/>whoever asked for it — announcing it makes the client<br/>ask again, which is a closed cycle with nothing to damp it.
    end

    rect rgb(255, 245, 250)
        Note over info,cc: PULL — second-chance refresh after a notification
        Note over bridge: A daemon notification often rides a phase transition.<br/>If that transition's push was lost, this recovers it.
        transport->>bridge: notification
        bridge->>transport: {type: request_tools} (debounced 2s)
        transport->>bridge: tools_update
        bridge->>cc: notifications/tools/list_changed
        Note over bridge,cc: This pull DOES announce — it sets no pending resolve,<br/>so the client never asked and the update is genuinely news.<br/>The client's answering tools/list lands in the section above,<br/>which stays silent. The exchange terminates.
    end
